* automotive_protection_models.lib
* Functional Qucs-S/ngspice models for a 12 V automotive input-protection front end.
*
* IMPORTANT
* These models are engineering approximations for topology, transient-clamp,
* reverse-polarity, and first-order stress verification. They are not
* manufacturer production macromodels and do not validate thermal performance,
* surge-energy capability, SOA, statistical spread, or exact switching behavior.
*
* ============================================================================
* PMOS_REV_60V — high-side P-channel reverse-polarity MOSFET
* Port order: D G S
*
* Intended circuit orientation:
*   D -> VIN_PROT
*   S -> VOUT_PROT
*   G -> GATE
*
* The body diode is oriented from D to S. With positive battery voltage it
* initially charges VOUT and creates negative VGS; with reverse battery it blocks.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT PMOS_REV_60V D G S

* Voltage-controlled low-resistance channel.
* The switch turns on when V(S)-V(G) exceeds approximately 2.2 V.
SDS D S S G SW_PMOS_60V

* Intrinsic body diode: anode at drain, cathode at source.
DBODY D S D_PMOS_BODY_60V

* First-order terminal capacitances.
CGS G S 600p
CGD G D 120p
CDS D S 120p

* Numerical leakage.
RDS_LEAK D S 1G

.ENDS PMOS_REV_60V

.MODEL SW_PMOS_60V SW(
+ RON=35m
+ ROFF=1G
+ VT=2.2
+ VH=0.2
+)

.MODEL D_PMOS_BODY_60V D(
+ IS=1e-12
+ N=1.15
+ RS=40m
+ CJO=250p
+ VJ=0.70
+ M=0.45
+ TT=30n
+ BV=60
+ IBV=100u
+)

* ============================================================================
* TVS_BIDIR_24V — bidirectional load-dump TVS approximation
* Port order: P N
*
* Built as two unidirectional avalanche diodes connected cathode-to-cathode.
* Approximate positive clamp:
*   about 27 V avalanche + forward diode drop + dynamic-resistance rise
*   typically around 30 V to 34 V for the intended simulation current range.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT TVS_BIDIR_24V P N
DTVS_A P MID D_TVS_24V
DTVS_B N MID D_TVS_24V
R_TVS_LEAK P N 1G
.ENDS TVS_BIDIR_24V

.MODEL D_TVS_24V D(
+ IS=1e-9
+ N=1.20
+ RS=250m
+ CJO=2n
+ VJ=0.70
+ M=0.35
+ TT=100n
+ BV=26.5
+ IBV=1m
+)

* ============================================================================
* ZENER12V — MOSFET gate-to-source clamp
*
* Connection:
*   Anode   -> GATE
*   Cathode -> VOUT_PROT / PMOS source
*
* It limits negative PMOS VGS during high battery and load dump.
* ============================================================================

.MODEL ZENER12V D(
+ IS=1e-10
+ N=1.15
+ RS=5
+ CJO=150p
+ VJ=0.70
+ M=0.35
+ TT=20n
+ BV=12
+ IBV=100u
+)

* ============================================================================
* Optional simple fuse-resistance subcircuit
* Port order: P N
* This represents only fuse/contact resistance; it does not simulate fuse blow.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT FUSE_5A_R P N PARAMS: RF=50m
RFUSE P N {RF}
.ENDS FUSE_5A_R
